ses  opportunities and threats and it also  helps you to identify well okay I maybe  I want to make this change in an  electronic health record but what does  that mean in terms of the regulatory  environment and the you know the  environment of who is controlling EHRs  and all this kind of stuff so it again  begins to open up your mind to  possibilities as well as things that you  need to do in order to get to your goal  it's going to be very useful road  mapping exercise so I will conclude with  this slide which is a kind of a collage  of various research opportunities that  we did both in terms of the VA and  primary care and the mobility research  we did and just reiterate that you know  we think that this this approach clearly  has value and at until you know we've  been using ethnography for many years  now and it's sort of recognized  company-wide that this has some value to  show in terms of the kinds of ideas and  the solutions that we come up with so i  think it's it's a fertile area for  anthropologists i know that there as i  mentioned other people who are also  involved in this kind of work who come  from a variety of disciplinary  backgrounds but i think i encourage you  for those of you who are thinking about  methodologies for PhD work you might  want to consider something like a bit of  an authority to help you flesh out your  your thought process some it's sometimes  works very hand in glove with more  quantitative kinds of work because it  helps to explain what's happening in one  realm or helps you prepare for the  quantitative if it is become much more  acceptable in terms of a unique kind of  our singular kind of research for  dissertation projects as well I'm happy  to see that more and more journals or  accepting research that's quantitative  qualitative and orientation so it  certainly has come to rise in academic  as well as more industry kinds of  evers so I think we have a fair amount  of time for questions so if anybody's  got any please